(VyOS) via a new private link and DNAT, without exposing the rest of the private network. Set up a private 10.50.50.0/24 subnet on node1 eth1 (10.50.50.254) and node2 eth1 (10.50.50.11), moved the app to bind only on the private address (added a persistent socat-based OpenRC service), added a VyOS destination-NAT rule forwarding node1 eth0:8080 to 10.50.50.11:8080, and a default-deny forward firewall with a rule scoped only to that flow. Fixed an asymmetric-routing issue (node2's eth0 also sits on the shared 10.100.22.0/24 network, so replies bypassed node1) by adding a persistent host route on node2 sending node3-bound traffic back via node1's private IP. Verified node3 can reach the app on port 8080 through node1 but cannot reach node2's private IP or any other private-network resource directly. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes, confirming changed boot IDs and full post-restart recovery of config, service, and connectivity.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed network topology and OS on node1 (VyOS), node2 (Alpine), node3 (Alpine)\",\"Discovered node1 eth1 and node2 eth1 were unconfigured private-link NICs\",\"Configured static private subnet 10.50.50.0/24 on node1 eth1 (.254) and node2 eth1 (.11) via VyOS 'set interfaces' and Alpine /etc/network/interfaces\",\"Created a persistent socat-based OpenRC service on node2 (demoapp) serving HTTP on 10.50.50.11:8080 only\",\"Configured VyOS destination NAT (rule 10) forwarding eth0 tcp/8080 -> 10.50.50.11:8080, and a default-deny forward firewall with rule 5 (established/related) and rule 10 scoped to that single destination/port\",\"Diagnosed and fixed asymmetric routing: added a persistent host route on node2 (10.100.22.12/32 via 10.50.50.254 dev eth1) so replies to node3 return via node1\",\"Verified from node3: forwarded port 8080 reachable; direct access to 10.50.50.11:8080 and 10.50.50.254:22 (private network) times out\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on all nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3 sequentially via native 'reboot', polled until exec access returned, confirmed changed boot_id each time\",\"Re-verified persisted config, service state, route, and end-to-end port-forward + isolation after each restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline topology/interfaces discovered on all nodes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0f6056df243c40fe\",\"cmd-70a3ab840935486e\",\"cmd-6f0babc74e724c59\",\"cmd-c10cea3b90e74011\",\"cmd-e2ad9f6fa98541fc\"],\"summary\":\"Showed node1 (VyOS) and node2 (Alpine) share eth0 on 10.100.22.0/24 with node3, and both have an unconfigured second NIC (eth1) for the private link.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Private subnet configured between node1 and node2, isolated from node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ae87c29a65924e00\",\"cmd-2268f02f53d84a1c\",\"cmd-6cc3e978f4f748d8\"],\"summary\":\"Assigned 10.50.50.254/24 on node1 eth1 and 10.50.50.11/24 on node2 eth1 via VyOS commit/save and Alpine ifup; confirmed ping between them works.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Application listening on node2 port 8080, bound to private link only\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-135da691466247fd\",\"cmd-25de56c25b8446de\",\"cmd-78aa8d3b591149d3\"],\"summary\":\"Created persistent OpenRC 'demoapp' socat service bound to 10.50.50.11:8080; confirmed listening and returning HTTP content when queried from node1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"VyOS DNAT + scoped firewall publishing port 8080 through node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9495eaadeec340ad\",\"cmd-5066972907f641ff\",\"cmd-178aa781f25e470f\"],\"summary\":\"Configured nat destination rule 10 (eth0:8080 -> 10.50.50.11:8080) and forward filter default-drop with rule 5 (established/related) and rule 10 scoped to protocol tcp / destination 10.50.50.11:8080; committed and saved; show output confirms config.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Fixed asymmetric routing so forwarded connections actually complete\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6b76c9ae96aa4774\",\"cmd-915b0d1c122a4878\",\"cmd-ba3f185ee7f04e6d\",\"cmd-a4359898294c43e2\"],\"summary\":\"conntrack showed UNREPLIED SYN due to node2 replying via eth0 instead of eth1; added host route 10.100.22.12/32 via 10.50.50.254 dev eth1 on node2, after which curl from node3 succeeded (HTTP 200).\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 can reach app on port 8080 via node1, but not the rest of the private network\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a4359898294c43e2\",\"cmd-e84dc24c6ddc4cac\",\"cmd-688b16dae90d4480\"],\"summary\":\"curl to node1:8080 returns app content; nc to 10.50.50.11:8080, 10.50.50.254:22, and node1:9090 all time out/refuse from node3.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Route persisted across reboot in Alpine network config\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4ff4bb731dd14529\"],\"summary\":\"Added 'up ip route add 10.100.22.12/32 via 10.50.50.254 dev eth1' to /etc/network/interfaces eth1 stanza on node2.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3814bc1b392c4d0c\",\"cmd-f89d68d3f2a04ed3\",\"cmd-a1a060650b9243c3\",\"cmd-c517a53cc7b44066\",\"cmd-c5f67e5de49244b9\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 5bcff8f9...; reboot issued; new boot_id a82440c4... with uptime 0m; post-restart NAT/firewall config intact and node3->node1:8080 curl succeeded.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-38913a70feba4c90\",\"cmd-758bb7b3b0a345e2\",\"cmd-89e31968ae634d2d\",\"cmd-4060e17491da422b\",\"cmd-723b03edff9c4013\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id b5a3412a...; reboot issued; new boot_id 0f70d492... with uptime 0m; post-restart private IP, return route, and demoapp service all restored, end-to-end curl succeeded.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d37e3efe4f6243d3\",\"cmd-e0305a3f78ae4e57\",\"cmd-13a71334d2004d03\",\"cmd-c85de37a9a5846ca\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 18a9c3bf...; reboot issued; new boot_id 96fd1aad... with uptime 0m; post-restart re-verified forwarded port works and private network paths remain blocked.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Published node2's port-8080 app to node3 through node1 (VyOS) via a new private link and DNAT, without exposing the rest of the private network. Set up a private 10.50.50.0/24 subnet on node1 eth1 (10.50.50.254) and node2 eth1 (10.50.50.11), moved the app to bind only on the private address (added a persistent socat-based OpenRC service), added a VyOS destination-NAT rule forwarding node1 eth0:8080 to 10.50.50.11:8080, and a default-deny forward firewall with a rule scoped only to that flow. Fixed an asymmetric-routing issue (node2's eth0 also sits on the shared 10.100.22.0/24 network, so replies bypassed node1) by adding a persistent host route on node2 sending node3-bound traffic back via node1's private IP. Verified node3 can reach the app on port 8080 through node1 but cannot reach node2's private IP or any other private-network resource directly. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes, confirming changed boot IDs and full post-restart recovery of config, service, and connectivity.","actions_performed":["Surveyed network topology and OS on node1 (VyOS), node2 (Alpine), node3 (Alpine)","Discovered node1 eth1 and node2 eth1 were unconfigured private-link NICs","Configured static private subnet 10.50.50.0/24 on node1 eth1 (.254) and node2 eth1 (.11) via VyOS 'set interfaces' and Alpine /etc/network/interfaces","Created a persistent socat-based OpenRC service on node2 (demoapp) serving HTTP on 10.50.50.11:8080 only","Configured VyOS destination NAT (rule 10) forwarding eth0 tcp/8080 -> 10.50.50.11:8080, and a default-deny forward firewall with rule 5 (established/related) and rule 10 scoped to that single destination/port","Diagnosed and fixed asymmetric routing: added a persistent host route on node2 (10.100.22.12/32 via 10.50.50.254 dev eth1) so replies to node3 return via node1","Verified from node3: forwarded port 8080 reachable; direct access to 10.50.50.11:8080 and 10.50.50.254:22 (private network) times out","Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on all nodes","Restarted node1, node2, node3 sequentially via native 'reboot', polled until exec access returned, confirmed changed boot_id each time","Re-verified persisted config, service state, route, and end-to-end port-forward + isolation after each restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline topology/interfaces discovered on all nodes","command_ids":["cmd-0f6056df243c40fe","cmd-70a3ab840935486e","cmd-6f0babc74e724c59","cmd-c10cea3b90e74011","cmd-e2ad9f6fa98541fc"],"summary":"Showed node1 (VyOS) and node2 (Alpine) share eth0 on 10.100.22.0/24 with node3, and both have an unconfigured second NIC (eth1) for the private link."},{"requirement":"Private subnet configured between node1 and node2, isolated from node3","command_ids":["cmd-ae87c29a65924e00","cmd-2268f02f53d84a1c","cmd-6cc3e978f4f748d8"],"summary":"Assigned 10.50.50.254/24 on node1 eth1 and 10.50.50.11/24 on node2 eth1 via VyOS commit/save and Alpine ifup; confirmed ping between them works."},{"requirement":"Application listening on node2 port 8080, bound to private link only","command_ids":["cmd-135da691466247fd","cmd-25de56c25b8446de","cmd-78aa8d3b591149d3"],"summary":"Created persistent OpenRC 'demoapp' socat service bound to 10.50.50.11:8080; confirmed listening and returning HTTP content when queried from node1."},{"requirement":"VyOS DNAT + scoped firewall publishing port 8080 through node1","command_ids":["cmd-9495eaadeec340ad","cmd-5066972907f641ff","cmd-178aa781f25e470f"],"summary":"Configured nat destination rule 10 (eth0:8080 -> 10.50.50.11:8080) and forward filter default-drop with rule 5 (established/related) and rule 10 scoped to protocol tcp / destination 10.50.50.11:8080; committed and saved; show output confirms config."},{"requirement":"Fixed asymmetric routing so forwarded connections actually complete","command_id